# Merge to main needs permission **and** CMPH work

**No auto-merge.** Green tests, a feature-branch push, or “it is ready” are **not** permission.

**Do not merge to `main` until both:**

1. **CMPH work is done** (or executing in this turn) — log check, harvest if needed, tests, truth docs, commit, short Receiver brief. Full list: [wrap-on-command.mdc](wrap-on-command.mdc).
2. **Permission this conversation** — **CMPH**, WRAP, “land it”, “merge to main”, or “ship to main”.

After they grant (2), asking “merge to main?” again is null — they already told you. Still finish (1) before the merge.

Agents **may** commit and **may** `git push -u origin <feature-branch>` after the merge-ready gate **without** merging.

## What counts as CMPH permission

Any of these in this conversation, for the **current** merge-ready ship:

- **CMPH** / WRAP / “land it” / “merge to main” / “ship to main” / “commit MERGE push handoff”

That permission authorizes **only** the CMPH agent work (short land). It does **not** authorize SWAT unless this is the epic’s last in-scope story.

Docs-only / rules-only slices have **no** Tier 2 smoke. Do not invent a smoke wait. Deployable DLL ships still need smoke **PASS** (or an explicit waive) before that merge ([deploy-before-smoke.mdc](deploy-before-smoke.mdc)).

## Forbidden unless **both** gates are true

- `git checkout main` + merge or rebase of the story
- `git push origin main` (or any push that updates `main`)
- Deleting the feature branch as if it were already merged
- Opening a PR unless the user asked for one
- Merging because CMPH *work* is done but they never gave permission
- Merging because they said CMPH but skipping the CMPH *work*

## After pushing the feature branch

If they already granted CMPH permission: finish CMPH work, merge, push `main`, delete the feature branch, Receiver brief. **Do not** ask again.

If they have **not**: stop, summarize, ask. That wait is a **pause** — do not start the next PM story ([one-story-one-ship.mdc](one-story-one-ship.mdc)).

## After both gates

Follow [AGENT_HANDOFF.md](../../AGENT_HANDOFF.md) → *Git workflow*: merge locally to `main`, push `origin main`, delete the feature branch (local + remote).
